      "content": "The straight-line depreciation method assumes a consistent expense value each year, which means the annual $8,000 should stay the same throughout the 10-year useful life of your CNC milling machine, provided nothing else changes, such as the salvage value or useful life estimate. This project management method is straightforward because it doesn't account for any potential fluctuations due to usage or technological advancements; it's based purely on time. So, as long as you retain the original estimates—which are often reviewed annually—your bookkeeping should accurately reflect a consistent annual depreciation expense with no adjustments necessary due to the nature of this method. However, always review company policies and applicable accounting standards, as they might require certain disclosures or adjustments, but these are typically outside the scope of straight-line depreciation calculations.",
